{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107839","id":2609562707,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6bisRT","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107839","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107839.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107839.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107839","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107839/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107839/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107839/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/56e04635a71f519ab0dab019d66773e8985e8652","number":107839,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Minor Optimization to Occlusion Culling","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B","html_url":"https://github.com/Rudolph-B","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Minor performance improvement to occlusion culling as well as a partial fix for #106184 (I'm working on something more comprehensive). \r\n\r\nThe performance gain comes from swapping one version of `Projection::xform` for another that is inlined. The two functions aren't a 1-to-1 match, so a minor rework the logic was required. After further testing, I believe the issue of small objects self-occluding (as described by @JFonS in #52545) was fully resolved in #94210. I’ve therefore updated the logic to be less conservative, resulting in a small improvement in occlusion rate which can be seen in the video below. The test [project](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20847878/occlusion-base.zip) is similar to the MRP in #106184. The camera is placed inside a box occluder, so ideally, everything should become occluded.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/30db2056-3115-4348-8b88-3556c7020dfa\r\n\r\nRegarding the performance improvements, I tested using [occlusion_culling_mesh_lod](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/3d/occlusion_culling_mesh_lod). On my machine, it went from roughly ~1.2 ms/frame (~830 FPS) to ~1.05 ms/frame (~950 FPS). Since this project is specifically designed to be bottlenecked by occlusion culling, I also tested using the [tps-demo](https://github.com/godotengine/tps-demo#). However, I wasn’t able to observe any noticeable performance improvement (~122 FPS before and after).\r\n\r\n>Godot v4.5.beta (b3d858fad) - Ubuntu 24.04.2 LTS 24.04 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 SUPER (nvidia; 550.144.03) - AMD Ryzen 7 3700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 14.76 GiB memory","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/g